        "articleBody": "There's a lot of chatter around AI citations, and it's easy to get confused about what's real and what's not. Let's clear up some common myths. Myth 1: You can track every single AI citation precisely. Fact: AI systems don't actually publish information about exactly what content they pull for a given answer. The models are constantly changing, so tracking every citation is pretty much impossible. We focus on maximizing coverage instead of chasing individual citations that an agency might claim to ",
        "datePublished": "2026-07-19"
